      "writtenOn": "2025-01-30T01:52:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Are they actually used in the sense that they are called by mainline code \non *current* releases (presumably that would be in PermissionMonitor.java)? If they are in use, then I agree we should have these constants. But if they are not - for example, if they are only used before Android T - then we should deprecate these constants, delete the implementation of the IPCs and replace them with:\n\n    DEPRECATED;\n\nlike we did, for exapmle, for bandwidthAddNaughtyApp.",
      "parentUuid": "f4d6f84f_ff90e68c",
      "revId": "90a0bd11c78b792d6337a30d13aca344061ef8a2",
